  "name": "TeamRetro: Log standups to Google Sheets and post a weekly participation report",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tr1800-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 780,
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Log standups to Google Sheets and post a weekly participation report\n\nFor scrum masters who want standup history they can search and trend. Every update from a closed TeamRetro standup is upserted into Google Sheets as its own row. Each Monday a second flow reads the log, posts who posted, new blockers and the longest-running blocker to Slack, and appends the week's numbers to a trends tab.\n\n### How it works\n\n1. **Daily:** the TeamRetro Trigger fires on **Standup Completed**. A delivery TeamRetro retries is skipped, so nothing happens twice. Each update becomes a plain-text row, upserted on Update ID so a row is never written twice.\n2. **Mondays at 9 AM:** the schedule reads the log and keeps the `days` days before today.\n3. A Code node counts standups held, who posted on how many, and new and long-running blockers, per team.\n4. Slack gets the report, and the week's numbers are appended to the trends tab.\n\n### Setup\n\n- [ ] Create a sheet \"Log\" with columns: Date, Team, Standup, Person, Question, Blocker, Update, Carried over, Update ID\n- [ ] Create a sheet \"Weekly\" with columns: Week ending, Team, Standups, People posting, Updates, New blockers, Longest blocker (standups)\n- [ ] Copy the Production URL from \"When Standup Closes\" into TeamRetro under Settings \u2192 Integrations \u2192 Webhooks, tick **Standup Completed**, and paste the signing secret back into the trigger\n- [ ] Connect Google Sheets and Slack, pick the document and sheets, and set `slackChannel`\n\nBoth flows have pinned samples. Running the pinned sample a second time stops at \"Skip Repeat Deliveries\": that is the duplicate guard.\n\n### Customization\n\nSet `includeCarriedOver` to false to log only new items."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
